## ubuntu-dispatch - NOT YET TAKEN (owed by plan 01 Task 1 Step G)

⛔ EVERY LITERAL PLAN 01's VERIFY GREPS FOR IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT FROM THIS
FILE. Step G requires an ubuntu section whose heading, run id, 40-hex head-sha
line, apt source, package version, ubuntu lane-probe line and job-outcome line
are all MEASURED. None of them has been. Writing any of those literals here --
even inside prose explaining that they are missing -- would make plan 01's own
`<verify>` chain pass on a section containing no measurement, which is the
control-that-cannot-fail shape this phase family exists to refuse. (Measured
while executing: a first draft of this very paragraph quoted the heading and the
job-outcome literal, and two of the three Step G assertions went green on
nothing. They are paraphrased below for exactly that reason.)

So plan 01 Task 1's `<verify>` is EXPECTED TO FAIL at the head-sha link until
Step G runs. That failure is the honest reading of this tree.

WHY IT IS ABSENT. Step G was DEFERRED TO THE ORCHESTRATOR BY INSTRUCTION. This
plan was executed inside an isolated GSD worktree on branch
`worktree-agent-a6b7676666dcd4667`; its commits are not on
`phase-164.4.1-pgcron-lane` until the harness merges them back, so a
`git push -u origin "$(git branch --show-current)"` from here would have pushed
the wrong ref and `gh workflow run ci.yml --ref ...` would have dispatched
against a branch the phase does not use. The executor did Steps A-F and stopped.

WHAT IS STILL OWED, and it is a MEASUREMENT, not a formality: 164.4.1-RESEARCH
assumption A1 -- `apt-get install postgresql-16-cron` succeeds on ubuntu-latest
and yields a PG16-loadable `.so` -- is INSPECTED, NEVER EXECUTED. Until Step G
runs, SC-1's ubuntu half is UNMET and plans 02-05 would be building on an
unmeasured provisioning step. Run it BEFORE dispatching plan 02.

Two readings of that run are NOT expected and each stops the phase:
  * the provisioning step itself fails (package absent, `.so`/`.control`
    missing, major != 16) -- SC-1's ubuntu half is unmet; do not work around it;
  * `sql-mutation` reports ANY defect kind other than `lane-blocked-stale` --
    that is a regression in Step C/D, not the tripwire.
A red `sql-mutation` whose ONLY defect kind is `lane-blocked-stale` IS the
expected reading of that run, and must never be recorded as a regression.

